@startuml qnx_dispatch_server_listening_activity
title QnxDispatchServer - caller-side listening lifecycle

start
if (Entry is StartListening?) then (yes)
    :Move all four callback arguments into the server members;
    :Construct QnxResourcePath from identifier_;
    :ResourceManagerServer::Start(path)\nDelegate native attachment to the shared engine;
    :Return the engine's expected result;
    stop
else (StopListening)
    :ResourceManagerServer::Stop()\nDelegate native detachment to the shared engine;
endif
:Return without resetting the stored callback members;
stop

legend
    All actions execute in the interface caller.
    Server construction copies configuration and leaves callbacks empty.
    The server destructor calls the same base Stop directly before member destruction.
    IServer forbids StopListening from server callbacks; stopping may block.
    Native request callbacks are separate from this caller-side control flow.
    No independent listening-state flag or duplicate-start guard is added here.
endlegend

@enduml
